quran[10]{c,v,t}:
  47,20,"The believers say: ‘If only a sura (i.e. a Qur’anic Chapter) was revealed (allowing fighting for self-defence).’ But when a decisive sura is revealed, in which (defensive) fighting is (clearly) mentioned, you see those with sickness in their hearts staring at you with the look of someone fainting at death. More fitting for them (would be)"
  47,21,"obedience (to God) and honourable words. So when the matter is resolved, if they remain true to Allah, that will surely be better for them."
  47,22,"(O hypocrites!) Perhaps if you were to take command, you would indeed cause corruption in the land and cut off the ties of your blood relations."
  47,23,"They are the ones whom Allah has cursed, so He made them deaf and blinded their sight."
  47,24,"Do they not then reflect on the Qur’an, or are there locks upon their hearts?"
  47,25,"Surely, those who turn their backs after guidance has become clear to them, Satan has tempted them, and he has deluded them with false hopes."
  47,26,That is because they said (privately) to those who (also) dislike what Allah has revealed: ‘We shall obey you in some matters.’ And Allah knows their secret dealings.
  47,27,"Then how (horrible) will it be when the angels cause them to die, striking their faces and their backs?"
  47,28,That is because they followed what displeased Allah and were averse to His good pleasure. So He has rendered their deeds void.
  47,29,Do those with sickness in their hearts think that Allah will not expose their malicious intentions?
